This appears to be a CBP ruling on a liquid-cooled EV charging cable assembly. Candidates are 8544.42 (insulated electric conductors fitted with connectors, ≤1,000 V) and 8544.49. The cable has connectors at both ends, so 8544.42 applies. Within 8544.42, the 8544.42.90 residual covers other cables, and the 10-digit statistical suffix is 8544.42.9090.

The one point I'm unsure of is whether CBP used 8544.42.2000 (the subheading for conductors of the kind used in telecommunications) or 8544.42.9090. Because the cable also has liquid cooling hoses, it could be argued to be a composite article, though the ruling most likely treats it as an insulated conductor with connectors. I am going with 8544.42.9090.

{"hts_code": "8544.42.9090", "reason": "The cable assembly consists of insulated copper conductors fitted with connectors at both ends and rated at or below 1,000 V, so it falls under HTSUS 8544.42 as other electric conductors, with the residual 8544.42.90 subheading applying."}
